Subject: CPMS I03C Semantic Residual Registry Justification

@ [justification_uuid] c23cef30-0dfb-4061-9653-f4e907eecae5

& [Need] public schemas deliberately name conditions they cannot express, but free residual strings do not reveal applicability current enforcement source identity proof status or authority limits
& [Selected] one compiled immutable catalogue with twenty stable records exact code snapshots and reconstructible reverse indexes
  + preserves the distinction between schema coverage residual applicability enforcement state and evaluation permission
  + makes every residual independently inspectable and queryable
  + detects code-binding staleness instead of silently trusting retained function names
& [Rejected] treating residual strings as documentation because spelling resolution alone cannot establish traceability or prevent stale claims
& [Rejected] treating existing tests as the registry because tests do not supply stable residual identity complete reverse indexes or authority policy
& [Rejected] storing current line numbers as authority because ordinary edits relocate code without changing semantic identity
& [Rejected] invoking enforcement during query because conformance observation must not inherit admission or execution authority
& [MixedStatus] I03-R020 records both enforceable zero counters and observational architectural non-capability so neither is overclaimed as the other
& [Decision] form the catalogue and proof contract now while retaining a separate activation gate for any Rust registry reader
